%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 7c7c947f0ccabb24dbf991df8e9f6d4f, type: 3}
  m_Name: inquiry oriented model of TE
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  defaultQuestions:
  - QuestionText: What is the central role of a teacher in the Inquiry-Oriented model?
    Options:
    - A technician implementing prescribed methods
    - A reflective practitioner and inquirer
    - A primary source of all knowledge
    - A neutral transmitter of curriculum
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: inquiry oriented model of TE
  - QuestionText: 'The primary goal of the Inquiry-Oriented model is to develop teachers
      who are:'
    Options:
    - Identical in their teaching approaches
    - Lifelong learners and problem-solvers
    - Experts in a single subject area
    - Efficient managers of classroom behavior
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: inquiry oriented model of TE
  - QuestionText: Which of the following is the core methodology associated with
      the Inquiry-Oriented model?
    Options:
    - Programmed Instruction
    - Micro-teaching
    - Action Research
    - Direct Instruction
    CorrectOptionIndex: 2
    LevelName: inquiry oriented model of TE
  - QuestionText: The Inquiry-Oriented model is most strongly influenced by the work
      of which scholar?
    Options:
    - B.F. Skinner
    - John Dewey
    - E.L. Thorndike
    - Benjamin Bloom
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: inquiry oriented model of TE
  - QuestionText: 'The first step in the inquiry cycle typically involves:'
    Options:
    - Analyzing data
    - Implementing a new strategy
    - Identifying a problem or question of practice
    - Writing a research report
    CorrectOptionIndex: 2
    LevelName: inquiry oriented model of TE
  - QuestionText: 'A key characteristic of this model is that it views knowledge
      for teaching as:'
    Options:
    - Fixed and universal
    - Contextually constructed through investigation
    - Solely derived from academic experts
    - Best acquired through lecture-based courses
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: inquiry oriented model of TE
  - QuestionText: Which of the following questions best exemplifies an inquiry-oriented
      approach?
    Options:
    - How can I best cover Chapter 5 by Friday?
    - What is the most effective scripted reading program?
    - Why are my students unable to transfer their math skills to real-world problems?
    - What is the definition of a noun?
    CorrectOptionIndex: 2
    LevelName: inquiry oriented model of TE
  - QuestionText: 'The Inquiry-Oriented model primarily aims to bridge the gap between:'
    Options:
    - Parents and teachers
    - Theory and practice
    - Primary and secondary education
    - Public and private schools
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: inquiry oriented model of TE
  - QuestionText: 'A major challenge in implementing the Inquiry-Oriented model is
      that it is:'
    Options:
    - Too quick and easy
    - Based on outdated theories
    - Focused only on low-level skills
    - Highly time-consuming and requires sustained support
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: inquiry oriented model of TE
  - QuestionText: 'In an inquiry-oriented program, assessment of teacher candidates
      would likely focus on their:'
    Options:
    - Speed in completing a lesson
    - Ability to conduct and present a classroom-based inquiry project
    - Score on a standardized content knowledge test
    - Adherence to a specific teaching method
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: inquiry oriented model of TE
  - QuestionText: 'The philosophical foundation of the Inquiry-Oriented model is
      most aligned with:'
    Options:
    - Behaviorism
    - Essentialism
    - Constructivism
    - Perennialism
    CorrectOptionIndex: 2
    LevelName: inquiry oriented model of TE
  - QuestionText: 'The term "teacher as researcher" implies that the teacher:'
    Options:
    - Should abandon teaching to become a university professor.
    - Systematically studies their own practice to generate knowledge.
    - Only uses research produced by others.
    - Is not responsible for student learning.
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: inquiry oriented model of TE
  - QuestionText: Which strategy is most aligned with fostering an inquiry-oriented
      approach in teacher education?
    Options:
    - Skills checklists
    - Competitive grading
    - Standardized lesson plans
    - Maintaining a reflective journal
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: inquiry oriented model of TE
  - QuestionText: 'A key merit of this model is that it:'
    Options:
    - Provides a one-size-fits-all solution to teaching problems.
    - Empowers teachers and increases their professional autonomy.
    - Ensures all teachers use identical methods.
    - Minimizes the need for teacher planning.
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: inquiry oriented model of TE
  - QuestionText: 'The inquiry cycle of "Plan, Act, Observe, Reflect" is central
      to:'
    Options:
    - Competency-Based Teacher Education
    - The Behaviouristic Model
    - Action Research
    - Mastery Learning
    CorrectOptionIndex: 2
    LevelName: inquiry oriented model of TE
  - QuestionText: 'In an inquiry-oriented classroom, a teacher would view student
      mistakes as:'
    Options:
    - Failures to be penalized
    - Data points for understanding thinking
    - Signs of student laziness
    - Irrelevant to the teaching process
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: inquiry oriented model of TE
  - QuestionText: 'Professional Learning Communities (PLCs) support the Inquiry-Oriented
      model by providing:'
    Options:
    - A structure for individual competition
    - A forum for collaborative inquiry and shared reflection
    - A way to standardize teacher evaluation
    - A replacement for university courses
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: inquiry oriented model of TE
  - QuestionText: 'A teacher investigating "How does the use of graphic organizers
      impact my students'' essay writing?" is engaging in:'
    Options:
    - Summative assessment
    - Aesthetic appreciation
    - Practitioner inquiry
    - Norm-referenced evaluation
    CorrectOptionIndex: 2
    LevelName: inquiry oriented model of TE
  - QuestionText: 'The Inquiry-Oriented model is a direct critique of models that
      view teaching as a(n):'
    Options:
    - Art form
    - Technical, delivery-based profession
    - Ethical endeavor
    - Political act
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: inquiry oriented model of TE
  - QuestionText: Which of the following is a necessary skill for a teacher in an
      inquiry-oriented program?
    Options:
    - Rote memorization
    - Avoiding questions
    - Blind adherence to curriculum
    - Critical reflection and data analysis
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: inquiry oriented model of TE
  - QuestionText: 'The primary source of knowledge in the Inquiry-Oriented model
      is the teacher''s own:'
    Options:
    - Intuition
    - Systematic investigation of practice
    - Textbook
    - Principal's directives
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: inquiry oriented model of TE
  - QuestionText: 'A potential drawback of this model is that it may lead to:'
    Options:
    - An over-reliance on external experts
    - Rigid teaching styles
    - Too much emphasis on standardized testing
    - A lack of immediate, clear-cut answers to classroom problems
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: inquiry oriented model of TE
  - QuestionText: 'The concept of "reflection-on-action" refers to:'
    Options:
    - Thinking while teaching
    - Thinking after teaching has occurred
    - Planning before teaching
    - Ignoring past experiences
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: inquiry oriented model of TE
  - QuestionText: An inquiry-oriented teacher education program would likely use
      which final project?
    Options:
    - A comprehensive written exam on theory
    - A portfolio documenting a complete cycle of classroom inquiry
    - A micro-teaching session on a random topic
    - A multiple-choice test on teaching methods
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: inquiry oriented model of TE
  - QuestionText: "Donald Sch\xF6n's concept of the \"reflective practitioner\" is
      a cornerstone of which model?"
    Options:
    - Behaviouristic
    - Apprenticeship
    - Competency-Based
    - Inquiry-Oriented
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: inquiry oriented model of TE
  - QuestionText: 'When an inquiry-oriented teacher shares their findings with colleagues,
      it contributes to:'
    Options:
    - Individual teacher ranking
    - The collective knowledge of the teaching community
    - Student grade inflation
    - Administrative workload
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: inquiry oriented model of TE
  - QuestionText: Which of the following is an example of data a teacher might collect
      for an inquiry?
    Options:
    - A list of competencies from a handbook
    - Samples of student work, observational notes, and student survey responses
    - The teacher's college transcripts
    - The school's mission statement
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: inquiry oriented model of TE
  - QuestionText: 'The Inquiry-Oriented model is least compatible with an educational
      system that emphasizes:'
    Options:
    - Teacher professionalism
    - Professional development
    - Collaborative planning
    - Standardized testing as the sole measure of success
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: inquiry oriented model of TE
  - QuestionText: 'A teacher educator promoting an inquiry orientation would ask
      student-teachers questions like:'
    Options:
    - '"Did you follow the lesson plan exactly?"'
    - '"What evidence do you have that your students achieved the learning objective?"'
    - '"How quickly did you finish the lesson?"'
    - '"Was your classroom perfectly quiet?"'
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: inquiry oriented model of TE
  - QuestionText: 'The ultimate beneficiary of a teacher''s inquiry is the:'
    Options:
    - School principal
    - Teacher educator
    - Student
    - Teacher themselves
    CorrectOptionIndex: 2
    LevelName: inquiry oriented model of TE
  - QuestionText: 'The inquiry process is best described as:'
    Options:
    - Linear and predictable
    - Cyclical and iterative
    - A one-time event
    - A fixed set of steps
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: inquiry oriented model of TE
  - QuestionText: A key difference between the Inquiry-Oriented model and the Competency-Based
      model is that the former emphasizes _____ while the latter emphasizes _____.
    Options:
    - skills; knowledge
    - process; demonstrated outcomes
    - theory; practice
    - content; pedagogy
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: inquiry oriented model of TE
  - QuestionText: '"Critical reflection" in this model involves examining:'
    Options:
    - Only one's successful lessons
    - The textbook's answers
    - Only the students' failures
    - One's own assumptions and the socio-political context of schooling
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: inquiry oriented model of TE
  - QuestionText: 'A teacher who systematically trials different questioning techniques
      to improve student participation is engaging in:'
    Options:
    - Unprofessional experimentation
    - Action research
    - Summative evaluation
    - Norm-referenced assessment
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: inquiry oriented model of TE
  - QuestionText: 'The Inquiry-Oriented model prepares teachers to be:'
    Options:
    - Dependent on external consultants
    - Adaptive to diverse and changing classroom contexts
    - Resistant to new ideas
    - Focused only on their own teaching
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: inquiry oriented model of TE
  - QuestionText: Which of the following is a "habit of mind" cultivated by this
      model?
    Options:
    - Compliance
    - Conformity
    - Memorization
    - Questioning
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: inquiry oriented model of TE
  - QuestionText: 'A school culture that supports inquiry-oriented teaching would
      be characterized by:'
    Options:
    - Fear of making mistakes
    - Trust, collaboration, and shared responsibility for learning
    - Strict adherence to a single teaching methodology
    - Isolation of teachers in their classrooms
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: inquiry oriented model of TE
  - QuestionText: 'The "O" in the "Plan, Act, Observe, Reflect" cycle refers to:'
    Options:
    - Obstructing the process
    - Officially reporting results
    - Systematically observing the effects of action
    - Offering opinions
    CorrectOptionIndex: 2
    LevelName: inquiry oriented model of TE
  - QuestionText: 'A teacher using an inquiry-oriented approach would view the curriculum
      as a:'
    Options:
    - Fixed document to be covered
    - Framework for exploration and investigation
    - List of topics to be memorized
    - Barrier to student creativity
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: inquiry oriented model of TE
  - QuestionText: 'The Inquiry-Oriented model is particularly relevant in the 21st
      century because it helps teachers:'
    Options:
    - Avoid using technology
    - Implement standardized curricula
    - Teach only basic skills
    - Navigate complex, information-rich environments
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: inquiry oriented model of TE
  - QuestionText: 'A "wondering" in practitioner inquiry is another term for a:'
    Options:
    - Final conclusion
    - Research question or problem of practice
    - Student's incorrect answer
    - Lesson objective
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: inquiry oriented model of TE
  - QuestionText: Which of the following is a limitation of the Inquiry-Oriented
      model?
    Options:
    - It is too focused on practical skills.
    - It ignores the role of reflection.
    - It produces teachers who are all the same.
    - It requires significant resources and institutional support.
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: inquiry oriented model of TE
  - QuestionText: 'The model''s focus on context means that knowledge generated through
      inquiry is:'
    Options:
    - Universally applicable
    - Specific to that teacher's classroom and situation
    - Irrelevant to other teachers
    - Only theoretical
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: inquiry oriented model of TE
  - QuestionText: 'A teacher educator modeling an inquiry-oriented approach would:'
    Options:
    - Lecture exclusively on research methods.
    - Avoid discussing classroom problems.
    - Provide a single correct way to teach every lesson.
    - Share their own inquiries into their teaching practice with student-teachers.
    CorrectOptionIndex: 3
    LevelName: inquiry oriented model of TE
  - QuestionText: "The concept of \"praxis\" \u2013 the integration of reflection
      and action \u2013 is central to which model?"
    Options:
    - Behaviouristic
    - Inquiry-Oriented
    - Competency-Based
    - Humanistic
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: inquiry oriented model of TE
  - QuestionText: 'In an inquiry-oriented program, a teaching portfolio would likely
      contain:'
    Options:
    - Only letters of recommendation
    - Only perfect lesson plans
    - Artifacts that show the process and results of the teacher's inquiry
    - Only standardized test scores of their students
    CorrectOptionIndex: 2
    LevelName: inquiry oriented model of TE
  - QuestionText: The Inquiry-Oriented model fundamentally shifts the teachers' role
      from knowledge transmitter to knowledge _____.
    Options:
    - avoider
    - generator
    - memorizer
    - receiver
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: inquiry oriented model of TE
  - QuestionText: A teacher who critically examines whether their assessment practices
      are fair to all student groups is engaging in which level of reflection?
    Options:
    - Technical
    - Practical
    - Critical
    - Superficial
    CorrectOptionIndex: 2
    LevelName: inquiry oriented model of TE
  - QuestionText: Which of the following best describes the relationship between
      the Inquiry-Oriented model and professional development?
    Options:
    - Professional development is unnecessary in this model.
    - Inquiry is a form of continuous professional development.
    - Professional development is only for novice teachers in this model.
    - The model relies solely on one-time workshops.
    CorrectOptionIndex: 1
    LevelName: inquiry oriented model of TE
